        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A synthesis method which consists of depositing a monocrystalline film (from a molecular beam) on a monocrystalline substrate under high vacuum (&lt;10^{-8} Pa). Molecular beam epitaxy is very slow, with a deposition rate of &lt;1000 nm per hour.</owl:annotatedTarget>
